  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDUCATION AND LOCAL LEADERSHIP FOR MITIGATING HUMAN - TIGER CONFLICT IN TADOBA ANDHARI TIGER RESERVE AND ITS PERIPHERAL FORESTS IN CENTRAL INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO REDUCE HUMAN - LARGE CARNIVORE CONFLICT AND FACILITATE CO-EXISTENCE OF PEOPLE AND WILDLIFE IN THE BUFFER FOREST OF TADOBA ANDHARI TIGER RESERVE. PROJECT OBJECTIVES INCLUDE, (1) EDUCATION FOR SENSITIZED AND AWARE COMMUNITIES OF 92 VILLAGES (2) LOCAL LEADERSHIP FOR MITIGATION, WHICH INCLUDES CREATING PRIMARY RESPONSE TEAMS IN 92 VILLAGES, WHO WILL BE THE FIRST RESPONDERS IN HUMAN-TIGER CONFLICT MITIGATION (3) PROTECTION OF WILDLIFE AND HABITAT (4) COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION IN MITIGATION IN HIGH CONFLICT VILLAGES AND (5) UNDERSTANDING TOLERANCE FOR BETTER MITIGATION PLANNING.</narrative>
  </description>
